35,2,1,talk,May,,"@Kenji @Mizuki @Midori @Servas The ledger shows thirty-four thousand yen in fees, and the complaint log reveals one household filed eleven of fourteen entries.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Mizuki"",""Midori"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,@May That concentration is telling. The station block’s minutes show they fractured over minor duties within two years. We must avoid that trap.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@May Thirty-four thousand yen is a lot! But the subsidy covers forty percent, capped at ninety thousand. We could save a lot if we fix the shelters properly.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@Mizuki That fracture is exactly what I fear. We need an arrangement that keeps us talking, not just sorting waste.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@May One household carrying most complaints is a warning. I found the truck arrives before dawn, and permanent changes take four months.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Servas Four months is a long wait. @Kenji If the subsidy covers forty percent, why are we still bleeding money on open bags?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@May The subsidy helps, but the real cost is social friction. We need a layout that prevents the daily resentment the station block experienced.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@May The open bags cause the fees! If we get proper shelters, we stop the leaks. The subsidy helps, but we need to fix the source first.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Midori,,@Kenji I agree. But let’s ensure the new setup doesn’t just shift the burden. We need a rhythm that lets us still share a smile over the fence.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Midori A shared smile is precious. But with the truck arriving before dawn, we must design a rhythm that respects our sleep and dignity.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"@Kenji If the subsidy covers forty percent, why are we still bleeding money on open bags?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@May Because the subsidy covers the structure, not the daily neglect. We need a design that makes proper use effortless, not just cheaper.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@May Exactly! The shelters cost two hundred forty-eight thousand, but the subsidy covers forty percent. We just need to stop the open bags to save the rest.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Mizuki Effortless is key. If the design feels like a chore, resentment builds. Let’s aim for something simple that invites cooperation, not just compliance.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,@Mizuki Effortless is wise. I worry about the four-month wait for permanent changes. We need a flexible start that respects our daily lives.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,@Kenji So we’re paying for neglect? I want a plan where no one’s gate becomes the default dumping ground.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,@May Agreed. The gate is a flashpoint. We need a layout that physically separates the waste from the private entrance to prevent that resentment.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@May I agree. We need to stop the bleeding. If we fix the shelters, we save money and keep the peace.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Mizuki I agree. Let’s keep the point neutral, away from any single gate, so no one feels targeted.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Midori Neutral ground is wise. But remember, every change takes four months. We must choose a rhythm that sustains us through that long wait.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
